```
**ADD THIS RIGHT BELOW IT:**
```javascript
  // 3. Fetch the roles from the database when the page loads
  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchRoles = async () => {
      try {
        const rolesData = await callApi("/JS/voucher/active-roles", null, "GET");
        if (rolesData && isMounted.current) {
          setDbRoleMap(rolesData);
        }
      } catch (err) {
        console.error("Failed to fetch roles mapping", err);
      }
    };
    fetchRoles();
  }, [callApi]);

```
### 3. Where it is used in the UI
If you replaced the View Modal code in the previous step, it is **already perfectly in place!** Scroll down to the bottom of your file where the Horizontal Stepper is. You will see it is automatically using the function you just added:
```javascript
  {/* Shows actual Role Name using our mapper */}
  <Chip 
    label={getRoleDisplayName(step.role)} // <--- THIS is where the state is used!
    size="small" 
    variant={isCurrent ? "filled" : "outlined"}
    color={isCurrent ? "primary" : "default"}
    sx={{ mt: 1, height: 22, fontSize: "0.65rem", fontWeight: "bold" }} 
